  "note": "Municipal elections, 17 May 1967. East Ward (five seats) was counted on polling night and West Ward (ten seats) the next morning (Banbridge Chronicle, 19 May 1967, p. 1); West Ward from the Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1967, p. 12 (round 2, 7 Nov 2026). Counted on Thursday 18 May 1967. The News-Letter prints Quail 379 and Plunkett 378 (Quail's figure is smudged; his name is printed 'Quaill'); the Banbridge Chronicle says Quail 'tied with Mr. Herbert Plunkett for the last seat in the West Ward and after a recount was chosen by lot'. The figures are recorded as the News-Letter prints them."
